      "verdict_reason": "Deceptive password capture, broad sensitive-store collection, configured exfiltration, wallet-app replacement and persistence tip the judgment. Installer packaging and an ad-hoc signature provide no legitimate explanation for those combined effects.",
      "execution_trace": "Universal Mach-O. ARM64 main at 0x100000690 obtains the decoded command and calls system at 0x1000006b8; x86-64 main calls its decoder and system at 0x10000065c. Independently reconstructed 37077-byte command using XOR seed 0x11667, multiplier 0x3785, 32-bit product and modulus 35999 (09:59:59). The result exactly equals both XorDecode fact strings, at file offsets 19600 and 85472. osascript evaluates the reconstructed AppleScript. It reads ~/.pwd or captures a masked Installation password and validates it with dscl. It copies Chromium Login Data/Web Data/Cookies, Gecko logins/key4/form history/cookies, browser extension stores, desktop wallets, login Keychain and hardware-UUID Keychain folders, Safari cookies/form values, Notes databases/media or Notes automation fallback, and extension-filtered Desktop/Documents files. A random /tmp tree is zipped by ditto, sent with curl POST --data-binary, and removed together with the ZIP. It downloads a Ledger Live replacement, kills and removes the installed app using the captured password, and extracts the replacement into /Applications. It downloads a command for a KeepAlive/RunAtLoad LaunchDaemon, copies/bootstrap-loads the plist with sudo -S, and falls back to detached nohup. Several operations catch errors; remote payload contents and actual runtime success are unknown.",
      "marker_note": "Mac Installer: phishes and steals secrets; add store-read profiles",
